 "reading": "K completeness separates the blocks at every cap: all 16-tag rows are 1.000, while larger-28 rows are 0.6105-0.8485 (margin 0.1515). But it is nearly invariant across caps: larger-28 moves only 0.0011 in absolute aggregate, and its per-seed range is at most 0.0121, while joint C1 passes move 0->0->4->8 overall and 0->0->4->6 in larger-28. K completeness is therefore a regime marker, not the cap lever. It also does not order joint success within larger-28: at cap 80, the lowest-completeness pass is 0.6568 while the highest-completeness failure is 0.7425.",
